From 88d7c460d452273037b346e92c33e2299937d2b3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 07:23:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] windowing/gbm: native output ends with the colour settings of
 that moment

The commit that gives the output back carried the colour range and the colour
format that were found when native output took it. A user who changed "Use
limited colour range" or the colour format meanwhile got the old ones until the
next change of mode of the window system, and the picture was washed out or
crushed in between.

The end now asks for what the settings say at that moment, in the same atomic
commit and before the first frame of what follows (CWinSystemGbm::
HandBackIntents()): for the range, CRgbRange::AtHandBack(), which reuses
CRgbRange::Wanted() with the value found as the value of the kernel; for the
colour format, OUTPUT_FORMAT::Stage() with the choice of the user, whose value
is now found by ChosenOutputFormat() for the staging of the ordinary frames too.
The depth of the link was already asked from the settings of that moment
(QueueLinkDepth()). A value that the driver refuses at the end is given up, said
in the log and not asked again, and what was found goes instead; while the
display refuses everything, every attempt carries it.

OUTPUT_STATE::CSnapshot takes these as intents (SetIntents()): what read-back
expects, and what the plan carries, in place of the value found.
